col (PPP), PPPoE provides an efficient way to create a separate connection for each user to a remote server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="93390">Point-to-Point Protocol over Ethernet</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="bn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="471820">পয়েন্ট-টু-পয়েন্ট প্রোটোকল ওভার ইথারনেট</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND, BGD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1000_93390_471821"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A specification for connecting users on an Ethernet network to the Internet through a broadband connection, such as a single DSL line, wireless device, or cable modem. Using PPPoE and a broadband modem, LAN users can gain individual authenticated access to high-speed data networks. By combining Ethernet and Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP), PPPoE provides an efficient way to create a separate connection for each user to a remote server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="93390">Point-to-Point Protocol over Ethernet</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="bn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="471821">PPPoE</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND, BGD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1000_93390_613750"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A specification for connecting users on an Ethernet network to the Internet through a broadband connection, such as a single DSL line, wireless device, or cable modem. Using PPPoE and a broadband modem, LAN users can gain individual authenticated access to high-speed data networks. By combining Ethernet and Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP), PPPoE provides an efficient way to create a separate connection for each user to a remote server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="93390">Point-to-Point Protocol over Ethernet</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="bn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="613750">পয়েন্ট-টু-পয়েন্ট প্রটোকল</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND, BGD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1000_93391_471820"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A specification for connecting users on an Ethernet network to the Internet through a broadband connection, such as a single DSL line, wireless device, or cable modem. Using PPPoE and a broadband modem, LAN users can gain individual authenticated access to high-speed data networks. By combining Ethernet and Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP), PPPoE provides an efficient way to create a separate connection for each user to a remote server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="93391">PPPoE</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="bn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="471820">পয়েন্ট-টু-পয়েন্ট প্রোটোকল ওভার ইথারনেট</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND, BGD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1000_93391_471821"><langSet xml:lang="en-US">