ank account holders in France that includes bank codes, branch codes, account number, and name of the account holder.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1993211">Relevé d'Identité Bancaire</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="bn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2005117">RIB</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND, BGD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34523_1993212_2005064"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A series of 6 digits used in Australia and New Zealand to identify banks and their branches and for routing transactions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1993212">bank state branch number</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="bn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2005064">BSB</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND, BGD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34523_1993213_2005064"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A series of 6 digits used in Australia and New Zealand to identify banks and their branches and for routing transactions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1993213">state branch number</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="bn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2005064">BSB</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND, BGD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34523_1993220_2005064"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A series of 6 digits used in Australia and New Zealand to identify banks and their branches and for routing transactions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1993220">BSB</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="bn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2005064">BSB</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND, BGD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34524_1993214_2005056"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A 20-digit number used to identify a Central Bank of Russian Federation account needed to facilitate international transactions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1993214">beneficiary correspondent account</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="bn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2005056">বেনিফিসিয়ারি করসপনডেন্ট অ্যাকাউন্ট</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND, BGD</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34526_1993216_2005057"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A 10-12 digit number used to identify individual and organizational taxpayers in the Russian Federation receiving funds through an international transaction.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><ter